      "side": 1,
      "message": "I don\u0027t understand this. Why is it not correct to return `hyp_ffa_version` in this case, as the code does already? The spec says:\n\n```\nIf it [callee] only supports a Firmware Framework implementation that is incompatible with and at a greater version number than specified by the caller, it must either return the version number of this implementation or the NOT_SUPPORTED error code.\n\nIt is strongly recommended that the callee returns the version number instead of the NOT_SUPPORTED error code.\n```",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 1522,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 1526,
        "endChar": 0
      },
      "revId": "0e78564953201e2928ff065d238c7fa78dfca6a7",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
